# Every tracked file checks out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true receives pattern
# templates and project-template files as CRLF. The engine tolerates that when
# reading, but the committed build bundles then differ from a fresh build by
# line ending alone, and any code that locates a byte offset in a normalized
# copy while slicing the original is off by one byte per line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The engine bundle is executable and must keep that bit in the index, or a
# Linux build reports a mode-only difference against the committed file.
bin/ai-saas-sdlc text eol=lf
